{
  "id": "unobtrusive-measure",
  "term": "unobtrusive measure",
  "definition": "An unobtrusive measure is an indirect way of assessing a person during an activity by using behavior that occurs as part of the task itself, such as the steps taken while navigating. In this context, it is used to estimate things like disorientation or learning-related performance without interrupting the activity.",
