      "passed": false,
      "reasons": [
        "The packet supports that an implicit/unobtrusive measure (lostness) can assess disorientation/learning by examining players’ steps during tasks, but it does not explicitly support the claim that it is used “without interrupting the activity.”",
        "The definition generalizes beyond the packet’s described use (VR educational games / hypertext usability) by stating it broadly as an indirect way of assessing a person during an activity, without evidence that this general formulation is how the source defines “unobtrusive measure.”"
